                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Why should this API take string as a parameter? Any specific reason for that?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 91,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "RekhaAparna01",
                        "email": "vrekhaaparna@ibm.com",
                        "username": "RekhaAparna01"
                    },
                    "message": "Output of read IM value APIs will be used as input for updating the IM value on planar. Return type of read IM value APIs is string so using string as input type parameter."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 91,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Why this API cares about the output of \"read IM value\". Also this API is not restricted to be used in continuation of \"ead IM value\".\nSo I don't agree with the argument above. Why should this api has the overhead of converting string to vector of uint8_t."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 91,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Discussed offline."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 95,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "If this has no use in the API, could you please check if in-place object can be passed to the API?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 95,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "RekhaAparna01",
                        "email": "vrekhaaparna@ibm.com",
                        "username": "RekhaAparna01"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 95,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "instead passing empty json, should we get the parsed system config json from the caller ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Why?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "RekhaAparna01",
                        "email": "vrekhaaparna@ibm.com",
                        "username": "RekhaAparna01"
                    },
                    "message": "Offset for system VPD is not present in the JSON. So system config JSON is not required to update the IM value on planar."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "The question was for @anupama.b.r1@ibm.com"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/src/single_fab.cpp",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "system config JSON is passed while creating parser object, to extract offset that EEPROM file. As Rekha mentioned, there is not offset for system VPD, so config JSON is not required in this case."
                }
